# Two Roads | INT | Tavern Back Room | NIGHT | canario, quincas | Be offered razors | A politician's money on the table. {quincas} wants blades in the game and votes delivered. {canario} takes the coin | | 4 | props=razor+coins
# Two Roads | EXT | Tia Bibiana's Yard | DAY | canario, tia_bibiana, dora | Be shown a dance | Drums for a saint. She has the children play slow, to music, gate open. He scoffs. {dora} sweeps him without touching him | {canario} is put on the ground by a child | 6 | crowd=40, dance, stunts=capoeira game, props=drums+paper flags
# Two Roads | EXT | Alley | NIGHT | canario | Win the wrong way | He beats the chief's best man, fair, in an alley. By morning three friends are on the boat for it | His victory costs three men | 5 | stunts=alley fight
# The Feast | EXT | Tia Bibiana's Yard | DAY | canario, tia_bibiana, vidal, dora | Play the law | The chief comes to arrest him and is offered a chair. The bow starts. {canario} plays the sergeant: never strikes, never touched. The man ends on his back, laughing | The art survives as a dance | 8 | crowd=120, dance, stunts=capoeira game, props=berimbau
# The Feast | EXT | Quay | DAWN | quincas, canario | See him off | {quincas} in irons at the prison boat. {canario} hands him back the razor, closed | | 3 | water, crowd=20
review: authored | 2026-11-12 | written whole; drawn from the criminalising of capoeira in 1890, with invented people
